---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { brand } from '../config/brand';
---

<Base
  title="Terms"
  description="Terms for using the Truth to Live By website and its editorial material."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <span class="eyebrow">USING THIS SITE</span>
      <h1>
        A few shared
        <br />
        <em>understandings.</em>
      </h1>
    </header>
    <div class="prose-page">
      <p class="small">Last updated: 26 September 2026.</p>

      <h2>About these terms</h2>
      <p>
        These terms apply to the Truth to Live By website. Truth to Live By is an independent
        publishing project operated by Mark Walsh in Ireland. Questions about these terms can be
        sent to <a href={`mailto:${brand.contactEmail}`}>{brand.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Editorial purpose</h2>
      <p>
        Truth to Live By explores ideas for general understanding and reflection. Content should be
        read in context, including its evidence notes and references. It is general information and
        does not provide medical, mental-health, legal, financial or other individual professional
        advice. Seek an appropriately qualified professional when a decision requires it.
      </p>

      <h2>Accuracy and corrections</h2>
      <p>
        Truth to Live By aims to treat sources fairly and distinguish evidence from interpretation.
        Ideas, evidence and external sources can change, and no guarantee is made that every item
        will remain complete or current. Use the <a href="/contact/">contact route</a> to flag a
        possible error, with a link and enough detail to examine it.
      </p>

      <h2>Content and attribution</h2>
      <p>
        Original site content and illustrations belong to their respective rights holders. Linking
        to an article and making limited use permitted by law are welcome. Permission for
        substantial reuse, republication or commercial use should be arranged with the relevant
        rights holder. Third-party material remains subject to its own rights and terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        Do not misuse the website, interfere with its operation or security, attempt unauthorised
        access, or use its content in a way that infringes another person’s rights or applicable
        law.
      </p>

      <h2>External services and links</h2>
      <p>
        The site links to beehiiv, YouTube, Instagram, TikTok, Facebook and other external sources.
        Those services operate under their own terms and privacy notices. Truth to Live By does not
        control their content, availability or data practices. A link is provided for context or
        convenience and does not by itself endorse everything on the linked service.
      </p>

      <h2>Owner-operated publishing system</h2>
      <p>
        The Truth to Live By publishing application is an internal brand-management tool. It is not
        offered as a public service and does not give website visitors access to social accounts or
        publishing functions. Its use of Google and YouTube services is also governed by the
        applicable platform terms and policies. See <a href="/publishing/">Publishing system</a> and{' '}
        <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Availability and responsibility</h2>
      <p>
        Reasonable care is taken in operating the website, but uninterrupted availability or the
        continued availability of any particular content is not guaranteed. To the extent permitted
        by law, Truth to Live By is not responsible for loss caused solely by reliance on general
        editorial material or by an unavailable third-party service. Nothing in these terms excludes
        or limits responsibility that cannot lawfully be excluded or limited.
      </p>

      <h2>Applicable law and changes</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by Irish law, without affecting any mandatory rights a visitor has
        under applicable law. The terms may be updated when the website or its services change. The
        date above identifies the current version.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
